  "description": "Blocked reason: Production code crash in ShoppingList.swift:rangeInText(for:) lines 85\u201390: content.index(lowerBound, offsetBy:) uses contentRange.lowerBound (an index in text) as a base index in content (a fresh String copy). Swift String indices are not interchangeable across distinct String instances. This crashes with \\\"String index is out of bounds\\\" whenever toggle() targets a line beyond the first few characters of a multi-line document.\n\nRemaining work: Fix production code defect in ShoppingList.swift:rangeInText(for:) lines 85\u201390: replace content.index(lowerBound, offsetBy: offset, limitedBy: contentRange.upperBound) and content.index($0, offsetBy: length, ...) with calls that advance text indices from contentRange.lowerBound (requires passing text as a parameter or changing content from String to Substring). Once fixed, re-run swift test --filter ShoppingListParserTests.",
